;; Regulatory source register for the ISIC mirror's authorities.
;;
;; This repository mirrors the UN's International Standard Industrial
;; Classification (Rev.4 per-class JSON, Rev.5 structure CSV) and measures its
;; own Rev.4 half against a second authority, Eurostat's NACE Rev.2. catalog.edn
;; records what the tables here CAME FROM; this file is the different thing --
;; the list of authorities a claim in this repository may be traced to, each
;; carrying the check that establishes it.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A source not in this table has NO spec-basis for
;; this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.kotoba`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; (The sibling ministry registers also carry :e-gov-law-id for statutes. This
;; register cites no statute: the authorities here are UN Statistics Division
;; and Eurostat pages, not Japanese law. The verifier keeps the e-Gov branch
;; and its self-test so the check stays exercised; no entry uses it.)
;;
;; HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path that
;; does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host in
;; the register on every run and fails if the answer has changed.
;;
;; Measured 2026-09-01: BOTH hosts answer **404**, not 403, for a path that
;; does not exist, with a real not-found page served at the requested URL.
;; unstats.un.org's is a small (1245-byte) IIS page titled
;; "404 - File or directory not found."; ec.europa.eu's is a large
;; (about 158 KB) page titled "Status 404 - Eurostat" carrying the full site
;; navigation. Neither host has been seen to serve a bot challenge to a paced
;; client, and 404 is not 2xx, so status still discriminates -- but a checker
;; written to expect the go.jp hosts' 403 refusal would misreport two hosts
;; that answered perfectly clearly. The status each host actually returned is
;; pinned in :host/missing-status and re-measured on every run.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in the register. Claims stop at the
;; level actually checked -- page identity, and for the :page-text pages the
;; strings read on 2026-09-01. No CSV, TXT or PDF is asserted as read, because
;; none was; the files themselves are catalog.edn's business, not this
;; register's.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.unstats-un-org"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "unstats.un.org"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "UN Statistics Division. A nonexistent path answers 404 with a
                1245-byte IIS page titled \"404 - File or directory not
                found.\", served at the requested URL. The title of that page
                differs from every real page on the host (which are titled
                \"UNSD &mdash; ...\"), so both status and title separate a real
                page from an invented one. No bot challenge observed from a
                paced client."}

 {:source/id "host.ec-europa-eu"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "ec.europa.eu"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "European Commission hosts, Eurostat included. A nonexistent
                path under /eurostat answers 404 with a roughly 158 KB page
                titled \"Status 404 - Eurostat\" -- larger than most real pages
                on the host, because it carries the full site navigation. Body
                size is not a signal; the status and the distinct title are."}

 ;; ── UN Statistics Division pages ──────────────────────────────────────────

 {:source/id "un.isic-landing"
  :source/kind :agency-page
  :source/title "ISIC classification landing page"
  :source/publisher "United Nations Statistics Division"
  :source/url "https://unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ/isic"
  :source/verify :page-text
  :page/title "UNSD &mdash; ISIC"
  :page/must-contain ["International Standard Industrial Classification"
                      "Rev. 5"
                      "Rev. 4"]
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-09-01"
  :source/covers #{:isic-rev4 :isic-rev5 :classification-authority}
  :source/note "The landing page data/rev5/upstream.edn and catalog.edn both
                trace the Rev.5 CSV to. The strings pinned above are the
                classification's full name and the two revisions this mirror
                carries. The structure files themselves (CSV/TXT) are NOT
                asserted here: they have no HTML title for :page-identity to
                check and their digests are catalog.edn's job."}

 {:source/id "un.econ-index"
  :source/kind :agency-page
  :source/title "Classifications on economic statistics index"
  :source/publisher "United Nations Statistics Division"
  :source/url "https://unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ"
  :source/verify :page-identity
  :page/title "UNSD &mdash; Classifications on economic statistics"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-09-01"
  :source/covers #{:classification-authority}
  :source/note "The economic-classifications index both cited pages hang off.
                Title only; its links were not enumerated, so nothing about
                which downloads it offers is asserted."}

 {:source/id "un.cpc-landing"
  :source/kind :agency-page
  :source/title "CPC classification landing page"
  :source/publisher "United Nations Statistics Division"
  :source/url "https://unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ/cpc"
  :source/verify :page-text
  :page/title "UNSD &mdash; CPC"
  :page/must-contain ["Central Product Classification"
                      "CPC Ver. 2.1"]
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-09-01"
  :source/covers #{:cpc :classification-authority}
  :source/note "The Central Product Classification, the product-side
                counterpart of ISIC, which PROJECT.jsonld lists in its
                vocabulary context. Cited at identity-plus-text only: no CPC
                code, structure count or correspondence to ISIC is asserted,
                because none was read."}

 ;; ── Eurostat (the second authority this repository measures against) ──────

 {:source/id "eurostat.nace-landing"
  :source/kind :agency-page
  :source/title "NACE overview page"
  :source/publisher "Eurostat (European Commission)"
  :source/url "https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/nace"
  :source/verify :page-identity
  :page/title "Overview - NACE - Eurostat"
  :source/retrieved-at "2026-09-01"
  :source/covers #{:nace-rev2 :classification-authority}
  :source/note "The page catalog.edn records as the route to the NACE Rev.2
                SDMX codelist this repository measured data/classes against.
                This register establishes that the authority's page is served
                and identified; the codelist itself and its digest are
                catalog.edn's business."}

 ;; ── What this register does not establish ──────────────────────────────────

 {:source/id "register.coverage"
  :source/kind :coverage
  :coverage/entries 4
  :coverage/by-verify {:page-identity 2 :page-text 2}
  :coverage/verified-at "2026-09-01"
  :coverage/covered #{:isic-rev4 :isic-rev5 :cpc :nace-rev2
                      :classification-authority}
  :coverage/not-covered
  ["Every data file. The Rev.5 CSV, the Rev.4 structure TXT and the NACE SDMX
    codelist are bytes, not pages: they carry no HTML title for :page-identity
    to check. Their digests, sizes and the three-way agreement between
    upstream, committed copy and recorded pin are catalog.edn's and
    data/rev5/upstream.edn's business, and are re-verified there."
   "Page content beyond the pinned strings. Which downloads the ISIC landing
    offers, what the CPC page says about correspondence tables, and anything
    else on the four cited pages is not asserted -- only the titles and the
    must-contain strings read on 2026-09-01."
   "Any statement that data/classes IS the UN's Rev.4. catalog.edn measures it
    as predominantly ISIC Rev.4 with localised NACE contamination and records
    47 disputed titles; this register's authority citations do not make the
    mirror more pinned than that measurement says it is."
   "A Rev.4 <-> Rev.5 correspondence table. None is linked from the UN landing
    page (catalog.edn records this), and this register cites none."
   "The COFOG classification. No COFOG landing page exists under
    unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ/cofog -- measured 2026-09-01 as
    HTTP 404 -- and this register cites nothing for it."
   "Whether either host could be read in a tight loop. A paced run (a few
    requests, seconds apart) was never challenged; no claim is made about
    burst behaviour, and the verifier fetches serially for that reason."]
  :source/note "This entity is checked against the file: the verifier compares
                :coverage/entries and :coverage/by-verify with what it actually
                read, so a source added without updating this block is a
                failure rather than a silent drift."}
]
